## Source triage pointers

- HTTP parser null diagnostics at generated httpd_parse.c:742/750 assume ra->sd is null at the defensive check:879. Actual IDF 6.0.2 httpd_sess.c:425-435 rejects a null session and deletes only after successful req_new. req_new binds ra->sd at 778; cleanup clears the request aux and sd. No reachable valid-session null trigger was found.
- Generated httpd_ws.c:120-130 uses a 25-byte key buffer and a 37-byte fixed GUID; concatenation destination is 63 bytes. native_httpd_headers.h:90-117 bounds copied header text and appends its terminator. The strcpy/strcat warnings do not establish an overflow.
- PDM multiplication native_audio_output.c:345 first computes 9*512=4608 before multiplying by 1000ULL. The warned intermediate cannot overflow. PCM conditional expressions at 210/418 promote already bounded int16 samples or ramp samples and zero to int before assigning int16.
- Legacy native_audio_output.c:780 combines I2S_MODE_MASTER=1, I2S_MODE_TX=4 and I2S_MODE_DAC_BUILT_IN=16. The actual compatibility header is C:/Work/yoRadio/.idf/v5.5.4/components/driver/deprecated/driver/i2s_types_legacy.h:114-128. Value 21 is the intended documented bitmask, not an invalid functional mode.
- network_settings.c:45 and time_settings.c:85 copy four-byte binary record magic after zeroing the entire record; these fields are compared as bytes, not passed as unterminated C strings.
- FLAC narrowings at 673/688/693/705/712 read only 4/2/4/4-or-5/5 bits. readUint:160-175 masks the requested width. readRiceSignedInt:192-237 bounds the uint32 folded code before returning its signed32 range, so assignment at 708 is bounded.
- Remaining warnings concern explicit Boolean string comparisons, sequenced short-circuit pointer increments, sentinel/zero enum initialization, enum storage size, duplicate branches, signed conditional promotions, or a status struct pre-zeroed before byte comparison at websocket_service.c:260/338. None supplies a concrete dangerous trigger.

